 "notes": "Creature catalogue in the creatures.json schema plus the D4 fields. Load like creatures.json (extend the loader to read data/creatures/*.json). Dragonflies: their larvae live underwater for years and eat tadpoles and small fish, so a pond's dragonflies depend on its water having stayed through the seasons; adults hunt insects over water and meadows and are eaten by birds. Venomous snakes: `venom.potency` 0-1 sets bite consequence — below 0.5 pain and a slow day, 0.5-0.8 serious and needs camp medicine, above 0.8 deadly without it; `sound` rattle/hiss/rasp is the audio warning most give before striking, and skittish ones only bite when stepped on — so sneaking and torchlight matter. Snakes hibernate in cold bands (den in rock), hunt rodents so they follow rodent booms near camps, and several live in the branch graph. 'invented' is absent: all real.",
